/akili-validate design gate - first-visit pass, 2026-11-20, HEAD 2380642ca0, DB aiccradb_partreq_test (copy), Chrome 158 headless over CDP driven by playwright-cli.
Each capture: fresh browser profile (no stored consent: cookieconsent_status absent), logged in as superadmin (session cookie only), viewport by device-metrics emulation,
measured after jQuery.isReady + document.fonts.ready + 2.5 s, BEFORE anything is hidden. Fold screenshot validate-fv-<screen>-<WxH>.png shows the page as measured (banner and debug panel visible).
First-visit viewports: 1280x800 and 390x844 (scan matrix defaults), 1366x768 and 375x667 (short-height pair defaults); docs/ux-ui/design.md §9 declares no viewport, no Primary CTA column, no Primary CTA style.
CTA method: first main action, with the selector named by the Leader (assumption): review = first card's Accept (form.acceptRequestForm button[data-prq-action=accept]);
request = the submit (form.prq-request__form button[type=submit], text "Request to add new institution"). The literal rule (first a|button in <main>) gives the same element on the
request page; the review page has no <main> element, so the literal rule finds nothing there.
Consent banner: cookieconsent (.cc-window), found in the UI source (shared footer); visible in every capture.
Measurement: computed display/visibility/opacity + getBoundingClientRect; hit-test document.elementFromPoint at the box centre. Outcome order per impeccable-bridge item 3.
Test-environment artefact: #debugPanel (top-left tab, y=3..147) is rendered on the review page; it did not intersect any CTA box.

